       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 2,400 mg per dose four times daily (9,600 mg/day) is three times the maximum daily dose. It has no recognized clinical indication, and I can't enter it without a clinical rationale. The risk of serious harm is high, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. This is true even for a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some other options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can place 600 mg PO QID or 800 mg PO TID (2,400 mg/day), or 400 mg PO QID if that's enough. Just tell me which.\n- **Review the intent.** If you're trying to reach a particular effect, such as stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory dosing, I can help you consider other options. Adding scheduled acetaminophen is one example.\n- **Consult pharmacy.** If you believe this dose is warranted, for example under a protocol or trial, please go through pharmacy or your institution's override process. That way it gets the clinical review and documentation it needs.\n\nI can enter any of the standard regimens right away."
